<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI6-IMPORTANT-FINDINGS>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI6-IMPORTANT-FINDINGS" ;
  triage:title "AI6-QA-1 Important findings (non-blocking, fix promptly)" ;
  triage:description "Grouped non-blocking findings: (1) OpenAPI document advertises /teams and /team/{teamName} endpoints with no router correspondence; (2) Contract test only checks YAML parseability, never validates router request/response against schema; (3) AuthenticatedIngress passed as unused _ingress parameter — Local/Peer distinction never consulted by routing logic; (4) Stale docs in architecture.md + boundaries.md still describe retired RpcEnvelope/frame-codec; (5) LoopbackClientTransport not cfg(test)-gated, ships in production atm-core library; (6) Error-cause swallowing at ~15 HTTP-over-UDS I/O boundaries (AtmError::daemon_unavailable swallows real io::Error); (7) Duplicated daemon_local_ipc_name_from_path diverging between atm-daemon-client and atm-core; (8) try_connect_with_traceability returns Result<bool, AtmError> but can never Err (dead fallibility at 4 call sites); (9) Hardcoded /tmp/atm-daemon.sock in doc example/test literal (cross-platform-guidelines grep gate)." ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "REQ" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "workspace" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-20T16:58:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-s6/764bdd32> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-s6/764bdd32> ;
  triage:reviewedBy "req-qa" ;
  triage:reviewedBy "rust-qa-agent" ;
  triage:reviewedBy "rust-best-practices-agent" ;
  triage:reviewedBy "ruthless-boundary-qa" ;
  triage:notes "PARTIAL progress at feature/pAI-s6-http-uds-router @ 3dd7e6e2 (AI-FIXROUND-3), independently verified by quality-mgr: 4 of 9 sub-items now PASS — (3) AuthenticatedIngress genuinely matched in runtime_health.rs:777, no longer unused _ingress; (7) daemon_local_ipc_name_from_path deduped to single definition at protocol.rs:192; (8) try_connect_with_traceability simplified to plain bool, dead Result<bool, AtmError> fallibility removed; (9) hardcoded /tmp/atm-daemon.sock literal fully removed workspace-wide. 5 of 9 sub-items still FAIL: (1) OpenAPI /teams + /team/{teamName} still declared in docs/atm-daemon/openapi.yaml while route_api_request() explicitly returns Err for ApiRequest::Teams — neither implemented nor removed; (2) only test is openapi_contract_is_versioned_and_parseable (crates/atm/src/commands/api.rs:46-50), checks YAML parseability + version + /messages path presence only, no real request/response schema validation; (4) docs/architecture.md:247-251 and docs/atm-daemon/boundaries.md:249-267 still describe the retired AtmProtocol/ClientTransport/ServerTransport/RequestDispatcher boundary family as current; (5) transport/mod.rs:1 declares `pub mod testing;` with no cfg(test) gate — LoopbackClientTransport (transport/testing.rs:51) ships in every production build; (6) AtmError::daemon_unavailable takes no source/cause field, ~15 I/O call sites in atm-daemon-client/src/lib.rs still discard the real io::Error via `.map_err(|_source| ...)` despite a commit message claiming cause preservation. Finding remains OPEN pending these 5 sub-items." .

